@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "employee.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki to OSB Employee Integration
	Testing employee sync updates in OSB caused by changes in Koroneiki.

Teardown:
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View Liferay employee
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	New Liferay employees who are added to koroneiki via okta should sync correctly to OSB.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"

Scenario: Remove Liferay employee
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	New Liferay employees who are removed from the Liferay Inc org on okta should sync correctly to OSB.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	When I remove the okta user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" from the okta group "Employees"
	Then the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should not be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should not be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"

Scenario: View Liferay Data Access US employee
	New Liferay employees who are members of Data Access US who are added to koroneiki via okta should sync correctly to OSB.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	When I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I assign the okta user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the okta group "Data Access US"
	And I log into the support homepage via okta as "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Data Access US"

Scenario: View Liferay Data Access EU employee
	New Liferay employees who are members of Data Access EU who are added to koroneiki via okta should sync correctly to OSB.

	Given I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | kor.employee1                    |
	| Email Address | kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken |
	| First Name    | KOR                              |
	| Last Name     | Employee1                        |
	| Group         | Employees                        |
	Then I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be synced to the support site
	And the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Employees"
	When I get all test passwords and admin emails
	And I assign the okta user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" to the okta group "Data Access EU"
	And I log into the support homepage via okta as "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" with password "${staticOktaUserPassword}"
	Then the support user with the email address "kor.employee1@liferay.com.broken" should be part of the support organization with the name "Data Access EU"